bove. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x = 0$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n2. $x =-1$ and $x = 2$ are roots of even multiplicity.\n3. $p(x) → ∞$ as $x → ∞$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233151 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22ff9dcd-4fa1-5c0a-bb5b-2eec3be880ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-112591" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b0ca55d089bea13471e9de6dd26093a1a9d477937106c92be26d5a469778c8a.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $x=-2$ is a simple root.\nII. - $x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\nIII. - $x=2$ is a root of even multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=-2$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the \n$x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=2$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=2$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29b26991-44b1-56a1-bf05-f64af923b565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244683} {:answer/id #uuid "5a49b8f8-15bc-5e9c-a83e-c2a6c2d407ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245106} {:answer/id #uuid "8be699b3-b4df-51fb-9167-5121af156c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245540} {:answer/id #uuid "da913451-65b0-54a3-ad54-758111c25aa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246258} {:answer/id #